---
config:
  flowchart:
    wrappingWidth: 400
---
flowchart TB
    accTitle: How a release moves a file of the project
    accDescr: An update of the blueprint leaves the files of the project as they are, such as the labels. Its pull request brings the step Files of the project of scripts/check.sh, which asks whether a release has left something to move. Where nothing is left, or the file declines the move, the pull request merges itself. Otherwise the check runs migrate --fix, and the fix bot commits the move onto the pull request, whose checks run again.

    update(["The pull request of<br>a blueprint update"])
    step{"Step Files of the project:<br>anything left to move?"}
    fix["The check runs<br>migrate --fix"]
    bot["The fix bot commits<br>the move onto the<br>pull request"]
    merged(["The pull request<br>merges itself"])

    update --> step
    step -- "no, or the file<br>declines it" --> merged
    step -- "yes" --> fix --> bot
    bot -- "the checks<br>run again" --> step

    classDef bot fill:#526cfe2e,stroke:#526cfe,stroke-width:2px
    classDef done fill:#16a34a2e,stroke:#16a34a,stroke-width:2px
    class update,fix,bot bot
    class merged done
